From 5cded6fd7c4bb80454b4aeb67b82a6403309728c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:32:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] multi-link: fix per-link metrics delivery for MLO client
 stations

Five issues are addressed for multi-link operation (MLO) client stations
that caused per-link signal strength and throughput metrics to be silently
dropped or written to the wrong data model path:

1. agent monitor: use affiliated link MAC as TLV 0xE4 key
   The affiliated STA metrics TLV must carry the affiliated link MAC as
   its station identifier, not the MLD MAC. Using the MLD MAC caused
   every link's TLV to carry the same key, so the controller's per-link
   DM path lookup always failed and metrics were silently discarded.

2. agent monitor: send raw bytes in TLV 0xE4 byte counters
   Per-link driver counters are already in bytes. Applying the BSS-level
   byte unit conversion divided by 1024 unnecessarily, causing the
   controller to store values 1024x smaller than the actual counters.

3. agent link metrics task: apply byte unit scaling for TLV 0xE4
   The affiliated STA metrics TLV must carry byte counters in the unit
   declared by the agent's Profile-2 ByteCounterUnits field. Add the
   missing scaling so the controller's inverse conversion produces the
   correct raw byte value in the data model.

4. controller: iterate all bssid_info entries in TLV 0x96 for MLO
   For MLO stations the agent sends one bssid_info entry per affiliated
   link. Previously only entry [0] was processed, leaving every other
   link's SignalStrength and EstMACDataRate fields at their default
   values. Iterate all entries and resolve each BSSID to the affiliated
   link MAC so each AffiliatedSTA DM path is updated correctly.

5. controller db: write link metrics to per-link AffiliatedSTA DM path
   dm_set_sta_link_metrics() and dm_set_affiliated_sta_metrics() were
   writing to the STAMLD-level station DM path instead of the specific
   AffiliatedSTA.{k} path. Capture the affiliated link's own DM path
   during the MLD MAC resolution fallback and use it as the write target.
   Fire vendor events with the affiliated link MAC so the steering
   application's per-link lookup succeeds.

6. Also fix the AffiliatedSTA.SignalStrength ODL schema type from uint8 to
   uint32 with a max-220 validator. RCPI is encoded as 0-220 per IEEE
   802.11-2020 Table 9-176 and uint8 caused silent truncation.

7. topology: skip non-1905 neighbor entry for known client stations
    MLO station MLD MACs appear in the Non-1905 Neighbor Device TLV because
    they are not 1905 agents. Adding them to the neighbor list prevents the
    station from being registered via the normal topology path, breaking
    metrics delivery and station connect notifications. Skip any MAC that
    already exists as a known client station.

8. controller db: register MLO station when MLD configuration report arrives
    The associated clients TLV from the agent may report affiliated link MACs
    instead of the MLD MAC, so the normal topology path never registers the
    MLD MAC. When the MLD configuration report is processed and the station is
    not yet registered, add it using the first affiliated link's serving BSSID.
    This ensures metrics events and station connect notifications reach the
    steering application correctly.

9. steering: use AP MLD MAC as target in client steering request for MLO STAs
    Per EasyMesh R6 and IEEE 802.11be, the target BSSID in a client steering
    request must be the AP MLD MAC address when steering an MLO station, not
    a link-specific BSSID. Resolve the link BSSID to the corresponding AP MLD
    MAC before building the steering request TLV. Legacy non-MLO stations are
    unaffected.

10. monitor: ignore ROC scan complete event when no pending measurements
    Both the monitor and the AP manager processes subscribe to the same nl80211
    multicast group, so the kernel delivers the remain-on-channel expired event
    to both. Only the process that initiated the scan has pending measurements.
    Without this guard the AP manager pushes an empty unassociated station stats
    event, causing the controller to receive a noise-floor RCPI value for every
    unassociated station query.

11. monitor: skip duplicate ROC scan request for already-pending station
    When a second unassociated station query arrives while a ROC scan is already
    in progress for the same station, skip the debugfs add to avoid a kernel
    EEXIST error. The in-flight scan will return the measurement when it expires.

12. controller: resolve affiliated link MAC when building unassociated query
    The station database is keyed by MLD MAC. When an unassociated query is
    requested for an affiliated link MAC, the direct station lookup returns
    nothing and the serving agent is not identified. Add a fallback that scans
    all registered stations for one whose affiliated link list contains the
    requested MAC, then uses that station's serving radio and agent. Also skip
    agents where the MLO station is currently associated, matching the existing
    logic for non-MLO stations.

13. controller: send single unassociated station query broadcast per request
    The previous path called the full station registration and broadcast helper
    once per qualifying agent, causing redundant broadcasts. Register each
    station in the database directly and send one broadcast after all agents
    have been processed.

14. Guard against a stale TOPOLOGY_RESPONSE STA MLD report from a PREVIOUS
    parent agent

Signed-off-by: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
